#: ../../source/docs/rover-motor-and-servo-configuration.rst:48
#: 5d013e4793c04e20890683d9cea6708b
msgid "Motor Driver Types"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-motor-and-servo-configuration.rst:50
#: 615c6788915c41668cddc2eb5f670dfa
msgid "At least three different Motor Driver (aka ESC) types are supported which allows using ArduPilot with most motor drivers.  The :ref:`MOT_PWM_TYPE <MOT_PWM_TYPE>` parameter should be used to ensure the output from the autopilot board matches the input required by the motor driver."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-motor-and-servo-configuration.rst:52
#: 04a505d75cd64965b64ed049928efb76
msgid "\"Normal\" is the most common and involves sending PWM values normally between 1000 and 2000 (1ms ~ 2ms) to an ESC. \"OneShot and OneShot125\" are variants of this (See :ref:`common-brushless-escs`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-motor-and-servo-configuration.rst:53
#: 6da45e1884e1499a965ce8b226f46fab
msgid "\"DShotxxxx\" is for use with DShot ESCs and uses a serial digital control stream (see :ref:`common-dshot-escs`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-motor-and-servo-configuration.rst:54
#: 4655f0e9d25646d39ce6f744491156a8
msgid "\":ref:`Brushed With Relay <common-brushed-motors>`\" is for brushed motor drivers that use a :ref:`relay pin <common-relay>` to indicate whether it should rotate forward or backward. Output is 0-100% duty cycle waveform."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-motor-and-servo-configuration.rst:55
#: d3d842a7dc1f475ab69123f71a010354
msgid "\"Brushed BiPolar\" is for brushed motor drivers that use basic PWM duty cycle to control motor direction and speed. These devices interpret a low duty cycle PWM value for full-speed reverse, 50% duty cycle as stopped, and a 100% duty cycle for full-speed forward. (Contrast to \"Normal servo control PWM\" where pulse width range 1-2ms is used for servo output position, and is only a ~5-10% duty-cycle overall.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-motor-and-servo-configuration.rst:57
#: 6c15740034e840728d9ea90b1d5761cc
msgid "Brushed motors are updated at the :ref:`MOT_PWM_FREQ<MOT_PWM_FREQ>` rate. Make sure that it is set at a value compatible with the brushed motor/esc you are using."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-motor-and-servo-configuration.rst:60
#: 1bc2fbdecaca47e08867962e78c76476
msgid "Reversing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-motor-and-servo-configuration.rst:62
#: 0d106f64517e4343b64610a65bfc4695
msgid "Rover vehicles may/or may not use reversing motors depending on configuration. If an ESC is used, usually 1500us is used to indicate idle for PWM and DShot systems. Brushed drivers this point will be 50% duty cycle, if reversible, unless the BRUSHED_WITH_RELAY type is used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-motor-and-servo-configuration.rst:64
#: faa8065e2b1f4e62bd893424678031fb
msgid "Some ESCs need a brief pause at idle as they change direction. :ref:`MOT_REV_DELAY <MOT_REV_DELAY>` can be used to provide that delay."
msgstr ""

