msgid "increase the \"Throttle %\" to 20"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-motor-and-servo-configuration.rst:91
#: cad17b602ab14c4b9b5d3865afa9002c
msgid "push the \"Test motor\" buttons to test the steering and motors."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-motor-and-servo-configuration.rst:93
#: 4b566bd1adc742e5976ad8149594cbf9
msgid "for rovers with separate steering and throttle, pushing the \"Test motor A\" button should cause the wheels to turn forward, \"Test motor B\" should cause steering to turn right."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-motor-and-servo-configuration.rst:94
#: f39b57f77e284238a9e29f24b1a099d5
msgid "for rovers with skid steering, \"Test motor C\" should cause the left wheel to turn forward.  \"Test motor D\" should cause the right wheel to turn forward."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-motor-and-servo-configuration.rst:95
#: 33015107d45d4e1084d416e327d48c20
msgid "If the motors or steering do not move in the correct direction change the appropriate ``SERVOx_REVERSED`` value and try again."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-motor-and-servo-configuration.rst:96
#: dd71b32be1cd4c6ea70478818cc1ac00
msgid "if a \"command rejected\" message appears or the motors or steering do not respond to the test, the cause may be written in the Mission Planner's Flight Data >> Messages tab (see bottom left of the window).  Common causes include the radio calibration having not been performed or the ``SERVOx_FUNCTION`` parameters having not been set correctly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-motor-and-servo-configuration.rst:101
#: 3b09eca97a6e4f5b95cbffe7489858ae
msgid "Minimum Throttle"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-motor-and-servo-configuration.rst:102
#: 831f8e1f2a114c459b78abcb9c382664
msgid "Many motors and ESCs have a dead zone. This is the zone between the zero throttle value and the throttle value at which the motor starts to move. This can be compensated by setting minimum throttle in the firmware."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-motor-and-servo-configuration.rst:104
#: 46b28bd0ed854fe4bc1d3f53ecab38f4
msgid "Remove wheels before proceeding with surface vehicles. Be aware of propellers on boats if they cannot be easily removed!"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-motor-and-servo-configuration.rst:106
#: 96278ef3d45e4a57a586a2841914b775
msgid "To fix the dead zone, open the motor test window in Mission Planner, as mentioned :ref:`below<rover-motor-and-servo-configuration-testing>`.  Find the minimum throttle value at which the motor turns on and set the parameter :ref:`MOT_THR_MIN<MOT_THR_MIN>` to that value. Now the motor should start at 1% throttle."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-motor-and-servo-configuration.rst:112
#: 4f54b5af819f4bd4852a272140bdc303
msgid "Steering Speed scaling"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-motor-and-servo-configuration.rst:114
#: 3e94fb6d12f84044b0d3fd38e308a03e
msgid "The amount of steering that a vehicle can apply without tipping due to lateral acceleration can be adjusted by changing :ref:`MOT_SPD_SCA_BASE<MOT_SPD_SCA_BASE>`. Speeds below this value will have the full steering angle. Speeds above will have the maximum steering angle reduced by the fraction :ref:`MOT_SPD_SCA_BASE<MOT_SPD_SCA_BASE>` / GroundSpeed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/rover-motor-and-servo-configuration.rst:116
#: 69dc7c890faf4bfbb4660de447784000
msgid "This scaling is used at all times in Acro, Hold, Steering, Auto, RTL, Smart RTL, and Follow. In Guided mode, it is used except when direct steering and throttle are provided as input commands. In Manual mode, the use of this scaling is enabled by the first bit of :ref:`MANUAL_OPTIONS<MANUAL_OPTIONS>`."
msgstr ""
